; Axis D (variant discriminant) — negative direction.
;
; The author writes a `bass`-only key (`:sequence`) but omits the
; discriminant `:kind` (typed as `kind-tag`, a closed-enum
; value-kind, which defaults to `kick`). With axis D off the
; discriminant is absent -> `missing_discriminant_key` at
; `[track]` plus `unknown_key` at `[track, sequence]` (no variant
; active means `:sequence` is unknown to the base form). With
; axis D on the overlay yields `kind = kick` -> variant `kick`
; active -> `:sequence` is a `bass` key and is still unknown ->
; `unknown_key` remains, but `missing_discriminant_key` is
; suppressed.
;
; The user-visible shift: axis-on tells you "you're in the kick
; variant; :sequence doesn't belong here" instead of axis-off's
; "the discriminant is missing." Both surface the same author
; mistake; axis-on names the active variant explicitly.
;
; `expected.sjon` matches the axis-off baseline (both diagnostics).
(plugin :name probe :version "1.0.0"
  (value-kind :name kind-tag
    :underlying symbol
    :members (member-set :values [kick bass]))
  (form :name track
    :discriminant kind
    (key :name kind :type kind-tag :default kick :optional true)
    (variant :when kick
      (key :name step :type number :optional true))
    (variant :when bass
      (key :name sequence :type any :optional true))))

(track :sequence [a b])
